JSBSim — https://github.com/JSBSim-Team/jsbsim
    JSBSim is LGPL 2.1. Its `c172x` aircraft definition is GPL, by Tony Peden.

    No JSBSim code is used here. src/sim/flight-model.js is written from
    scratch. What IS taken is measured data: the geometry, inertias and
    stability derivatives of a 1982 Cessna 172P, converted to SI from the
    c172x definition and listed in the AIRCRAFT constant.

    These are physical measurements of a real aircraft rather than authored
    expression, and they are used as facts. The c172x file states of itself
    that it "models a 1982 Cessna 172P based on publicly available data and
    technical resources" — so the underlying figures are drawn from public
    sources, and what is reused here is those figures, not their arrangement,
    their surrounding XML, or any part of the JSBSim engine.

    They are credited here and on the in-app Sources page because they are the
    expensive half of any flight model, they took a wind tunnel and a flight
    test programme that this project could never have run, and the honest
    division of labour in this subject is that the mathematics is free while
    the coefficients cost a fortune.

